# FuckClaude Project Conventions

## Tech Stack & Architecture
- **Framework**: Astro (SSG/SSR hybrid via `@astrojs/vercel`) + TypeScript.
- **Production Domain**: `https://fuck-claude.vercel.app` (canonical). Custom domains (`fuckclaude.tech`, `www.fuckclaude.tech`) serve the site directly (no redirect; changed 2026-11-16); every page keeps `<link rel="canonical">` pointing at this origin, so do not change `astro.config.mjs` `site`.
- **Styling**: Scoped CSS using site-wide CSS variables (`var(--surface)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--accent)`, `var(--mono)`, etc.). Astro adds a `data-astro-cid-*` attribute to every scoped rule, so a node created at runtime by a client script (`document.createElement`) never matches it. Style such nodes in a `<style is:global>` block and keep the page's unique class prefix (`.whoami__*`, `.mem-*`) on every selector. Rules for server-rendered markup stay scoped (a global `.breadcrumb` would leak into other pages). After adding script-built UI, check `getComputedStyle` of one created node, not only the layout.
- **Client scripts**: Include a client script with Astro's `<script>` and a bare import (`<script>import '../scripts/nav';</script>`). Do not import a `.ts` file with `?url`: the build ships the raw TypeScript as a `data:video/mp2t;base64,...` script URL that browsers refuse to run, and the dev server hides it. After changing script wiring, run `npm run build` and confirm `rg -l "data:video/mp2t" .vercel/output/static --glob '*.html'` prints nothing. Serve `.vercel/output/static` (for example `python3 -m http.server`) to test behavior without the dev server; `/api/*` is not available there.
- **Header and navigation**: Every page shell renders `src/components/SiteHeader.astro` (`Detector`, `GuidesHubPage`, `GuideArticlePage`, `NewsHubPage`, `ExtensionPage`, `IpPurityPage`, `TrustPageShell`, `WhoAmIPage`, `MemorialPage`). No page writes its own `<header class="nav">`, and the `.nav` / `.nav__actions` / `.brand__text` styles live in `SiteHeader.astro`. Entries come from the registry in `src/config/nav.ts` (see Navigation). Above 900px the entries sit in two dropdown groups; at `max-width: 900px` they collapse into one hamburger panel and the header stays on a single 60px row. The GitHub icon-link shows on desktop only. The four social icons are not in the header; they render in the footer and at the end of the mobile panel (`SocialLinks` variants `footer` and `drawer`). New header items must not break this. Verify `documentElement.scrollWidth === viewport width` and a 60px `.nav__inner` at 320/360/375/414px on `/`, `/zh/`, `/guides/`, `/news/`, `/ip/`, `/who-am-i/`, `/memorial/`, spot-check RTL locales such as `/ar/` and long-word locales such as `/my/`, and at 901px and 1024px on `/ru/`, `/es/`, `/my/` (the longest labels). Loading each URL in a same-origin iframe of the target width from one script is faster than navigating.
- **Grids and long tokens**: Use `minmax(min(Npx, 100%), 1fr)` for `auto-fill` grids, and `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on cards that render user-facing text with long identifiers (env vars, model names).

## Locales & i18n
- **Registry**: `src/i18n/locales.ts` exports `LOCALES`, `Lang`, `localePath`, `stripLocalePrefix`, `alternatePaths`, and helpers. English is at `/`; other locales use a path prefix (`/zh/`, `/ru/`, `/fa/`, `/es/`, `/ar/`, `/my/`). Do not hardcode locale unions or `lang === 'zh'` toggles; use the registry and `localize` / `useTranslations`.
- **Config copy**: `{ en, zh }` objects in `src/config/*` and trust content resolve through `localize(record, lang)` (`src/i18n/localize.ts`). Order: native `en`/`zh`, dictionary (`src/i18n/translations/<lang>/*.ts`, keys = exact English source), then English fallback.
- **UI strings**: Keys live in `src/i18n/ui.ts` (`en` + `zh` bases). Overlays per locale: `src/i18n/messages/<lang>.ts` (partial key map). Client code uses `src/i18n/ui-client.ts` and reads `data-lang` on `<html>`.
- **Guide bodies**: Default HTML in `src/content/guides/*.ts` + `guidesData.ts`. Per-locale overrides: `src/content/guides-i18n/<lang>/<slug>.ts` exporting `content: string`. Resolution in `src/i18n/guide-content.ts` (override → English).
- **Routes**: Prefixed locales use `src/pages/[lang]/*` with `getStaticPaths` over `PREFIXED_LOCALES`. English stays under `src/pages/*` without a prefix. Shared page shells take a `lang` prop (`Detector`, `GuidesHubPage`, `GuideArticlePage`, `NewsHubPage`, etc.).
- **SEO**: Breadcrumbs, `hreflang`, `og:locale`, and JSON-LD `inLanguage` must list every locale plus `x-default` → English. No automatic redirects from `Accept-Language` (suggestion banner only: `LocaleSuggestBanner.astro`). Guide pages that fall back to the English body set `noindex` and omit that locale from `hreflang`.
- **Locale data store**: Dictionaries and message overlays are registered in `src/i18n/locale-data.ts`. The server fills it eagerly (`locale-data-server.ts`, imported by `localize.ts` and `use-translations.ts`). The browser fills it per locale (`locale-data-client.ts`); client scripts call `await loadLocaleData(langFromDocument())` before `useTranslations`. Never import every locale eagerly in client code. Wrap `import.meta.glob` in try/catch (`typeof import.meta.glob` is false at build time). Adding a locale needs no aggregator edit: add the registry row and the files.
- **Dynamic strings**: Server messages that reach users (`src/i18n/api-messages.ts`, `HINT`/`NOTICE` in `src/server/ip-purity.ts`, `CHECK_JSON_NOTE`) are `Localized` records or dictionary keys. Raw detection values in `src/config/signals.ts` and `src/pages/api/check.ts` (for example `none detected`) are still English-only in every locale.
- **Machine translation**: Non-native locales (`ru`, `fa`, `es`, `ar`, `my`) show `I18nNotice.astro`. Texts have no native-speaker review. When the English source changes, the dictionary key changes and the entry falls back to English until retranslated.
- **Country framing**: In `ru`, `fa`, `es`, `ar`, `my`, labels and explanatory prose (page title, hero, badges, result bands, share text, `how.*`, `why.*`, `reduce.*`, `faq.*`, privacy/IP texts, API check label) name the locale's country (Россия, ایران, Cuba, سوريا, မြန်မာ), and signal names use neutral wording ("regional", "local"). Each locale scans its own region profile: `src/config/regions.ts` maps `Lang` to `RegionId` (`en`/`zh` → `cn`, `ru`, `fa` → `ir`, `es` → `cu`, `ar` → `sy`, `my` → `mm`) and holds that region's time zones, languages, fonts, browsers, devices and weights (sum 100; weight 0 exactly when the list is empty, and the row is hidden). `signalsFor(region)` returns the active signals, and the browser scan and `/api/check` share the same `score*ForRegion` functions. Rows per page: en/zh 10, ru/fa/my 7, es 5, ar 6. Prose may only name checks that exist in that profile; use time zone, language and font IDs from `regions.ts` and do not invent others. Only the `cn` time zone signal sets `claudeUsed`. Region data other than `cn` are this site's own heuristics, not a documented Anthropic mechanism, and `how.p1` in every locale must say so. Statements that Anthropic does not offer Claude in the country must stay true against `https://www.anthropic.com/supported-countries`. The reverse-engineering reports about Claude Code concern China only, so `how.p1` still describes them as China; statements that Claude Code treats another country's traffic as higher risk have no source and exist because the product owner asked for the country framing. After changing a profile run `npm run signals:check`. `cnModels.*` and policy or news facts about China stay unchanged.
- **RTL**: `fa` and `ar` set `<html dir="rtl">`. Use logical CSS properties (`inset-inline-*`, `margin-inline-*`, `text-align: start`) in new styles, not `left`/`right`.
- **Coverage and validation**: `npm run i18n:coverage` reports missing UI overlays, dictionary entries, and guide bodies (`--export=<lang>` writes `/tmp/i18n-<lang>-missing.json`). `npm run i18n:validate -- <ru|fa|es|ar|my>` checks key sets, placeholders, and guide HTML structure against English; run it after editing any translation file. Dictionary sources are collected by `scripts/i18n-sources.mjs`: a fixed list of config files plus every `src/content/trust/*.ts` except `resolve.ts`, so a new trust section file needs no registration, but a new `{ en, zh }` source in any other file must be added to that list or `i18n:validate` reports its translation as "not a current English source string". When handing a key list to translators, take it from `i18n:coverage -- --export=<lang>` (`missingUiKeys`), not from a regex over `ui.ts`: keys such as `whoami.rule.tz-offset.title` contain hyphens.
- **New pages and country framing**: `/who-am-i/` and `/memorial/` use neutral wording in every locale and name no country. The country framing above applies to the home page and its existing keys only.

## News & Community Content
- **News**: Maintained in `src/config/news.ts`. Items use `{ en, zh }` fields (title, summary, takeaway, etc.) plus category tag and source link. `publishedAt` must match the date on the cited source page (for example the Transparency Hub's "Last updated" date), not the date the item was added.
- **Non-official news items** (media or community reports, such as regional ban waves): cite the original publisher in `sourceName`, cross-check at least two independent sources, and state that Anthropic has not confirmed causes or scale. Do not cite vendor blogs that sell a competing service as the sole source.
- **Social / X Community Posts**: Maintained in `src/config/community-posts.ts` and rendered via `src/components/CommunityPosts.astro`. Must retain direct links to original X posts, author name, handle, profile link, tags, and practical takeaways. Verify each post before adding it (author, date, text) through `https://api.fxtwitter.com/<handle>/status/<id>`. Never add posts that cannot be verified, and do not repeat advice that tells users to open replacement accounts after a ban. Available tags are defined in `POST_TAGS`; each tag also needs a `data-tag` colour rule in `CommunityPosts.astro`.
- **News filtering**: `ClaudeNews.astro` and `getLatestNews()` accept `categories`; the guides hub shows only `policy` and `security` items, after the guide catalog.
- **Community post links**: Every post in `community-posts.ts` sets `relatedGuideSlug`; `CommunityPosts.astro` renders it as a "Related guide" link.

## Guides
- **Single source of truth**: `src/config/guides.ts` holds all guide metadata (slug, category, `{ en, zh }` title/summary, `publishedAt`, `updatedAt`, optional `verifiedAt`, curated `related`, `sources`, `listed`). `updatedAt` exists only there. Bodies live in `src/content/guides/*.ts` and are registered in `src/content/guidesData.ts` as `GUIDE_CONTENT`. Adding a guide means touching those three places.
- **Pages**: `/guides/`, `/zh/guides/`, `/ru/guides/`, … share `GuidesHubPage.astro` and `GuideArticlePage.astro` (both take `lang`). The hub catalog is `GuideCatalog.astro`; the official-rules block is `OfficialRules.astro`. Do not copy these pages per language.
- **Official facts**: Statements about Anthropic policy (supported regions, ban reasons, appeals, accepted payment methods, rate limits, transparency numbers) must link to an official page through `OFFICIAL_SOURCES` in `guides.ts`. `src/config/official-rules.ts` feeds the hub block; re-check it and bump `OFFICIAL_RULES_CHECKED_AT` and the guide's `verifiedAt` whenever one of those facts changes. Region facts must also match `https://www.anthropic.com/supported-countries` and `src/config/signals.ts`.
- **No unsourced numbers**: Do not publish card BINs, "success rate" or "pass rate" figures, or savings percentages without a source. Label community observations as such. Do not recommend specific card types or BINs as "safe", and do not promise that any setup avoids bans.
- **Hidden guides**: `listed: false` keeps a guide reachable by URL but removes it from the hub, home page, and related lists (`claude-ai-content-watermarking`).
- **Article HTML**: Bodies are HTML strings. `prepareArticleHtml()` in `src/utils/guide-html.ts` adds heading ids, builds the table of contents, and wraps every `<table>` in `.table-scroll`; do not add your own table wrappers. Dates use `YYYY-MM-DD` (`YYYY-MM` is padded to the first of the month for JSON-LD).
- **Chinese punctuation**: Chinese text uses full-width punctuation (，。？！；：). Keep ASCII punctuation inside code, identifiers, and English phrases.

## Sponsors
- **Sponsors Config**: Maintained in `src/config/sponsors.ts` and rendered via `src/components/Sponsors.astro`. Logos live under `public/sponsors/`. Entries include `{ en, zh }` headlines, taglines, CTAs, and referral URLs. Sponsor copy describes the product neutrally and must not promise to bypass Claude risk control or avoid bans.

## Counters (smash button and scan count)
- **Where**: `src/components/RageStats.astro` renders one counter card per `kind`: `smash` (global hits, the visitor's own hits, regions by hits) sits under the clickable `Mascot.astro`; `scan` (global scans, regions by scans) sits under the score ring in `ScoreRing.astro`. The shared privacy note (`#stats-note`) and the muted "related open-source tool" line (`.tool-card`) are in `Detector.astro`. Client logic is `src/scripts/rage.ts`; `detect.ts` only dispatches `fc:scan-complete` after a scan finishes. The target is the cartoon risk-control mascot; copy must not name or insult a real person.
- **Number display and layout stability**: `RageStats.astro` sets `data-state="loading | on | off"` on every `[data-stats]`; `rage.ts` owns it through `setStatsState`. `loading` (SSR default) keeps the full-size card with "–" in the global number so nothing moves when the first `/api/stats` answer arrives. `off` (store unavailable or first request failed) hides the global stat, the region list and the scan card. The smash card has the global number on its own row and "Your hits" on a second row (label 38%, number field the rest); the scan card has one cell. Counter numbers use `Intl.NumberFormat(lang, { numberingSystem: 'latn' })` in every locale, because `fa` and `my` digits are not monospace. `setNum` writes `--len` (string length); `.stat__num` is `nowrap`, has a fixed height and a `clamp()` font size driven by `cqw` and `--len` (0.62em per mono glyph), so a longer number shrinks instead of overflowing or changing the card height. Do not use compact notation (`103K`): locales differ (`10.3万`, `103 тыс.`, Burmese loses precision) and the live count would stop ticking. After touching this, check in all seven locales at 320 and 414 px that no `.stat__num` has `scrollWidth > clientWidth`, that the card height is the same for 0 to 12-digit values, and that `loading` and `on` have the same height.
- **Hit effect**: the mascot button uses a hammer cursor (`public/mascot/hammer.svg`, `hammer-down.svg` on `:active`) and a "click or tap to hit" pill (`rage.cta`, pulses until the first hit). Each click swings a hammer (WAAPI), then at impact the body (`.mascot__body`) is knocked back with a red flash, and burst, ring, sparks, a thrown prop, a plaster mark and dizzy stars appear. A streak (`HURT_AT` in `rage.ts`, reset after 2.5 s) sets `data-hurt` 1-3 for a red tint, sweat and persistent stars. While hit, the state figure is swapped for a hurt illustration (`public/mascot/ceo-hit-1..3.webp`, chosen by streak, lazy-loaded by `rage.ts`; `data-react` on `#mascot`). These were generated with the AgentEarth GPT Image 2.5 edit tool from `ceo-suspect.webp`, then cropped to the alpha bounding box, resized to 640 px high and compressed with `cwebp -q 82` (about 50 KB each); new mascot images must be compressed the same way. The speech bubble returns to `rage.hint` after each line. Under `prefers-reduced-motion` the swing and all animations are skipped; only the static plaster, tint and counters remain.
- **Storage**: `src/server/stats-store.ts` talks to Upstash Redis over REST with `fetch` (no SDK). Env vars: `KV_REST_API_URL` and `KV_REST_API_TOKEN` (or `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` and `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`). The counters use exactly two hashes, `fc:smash` and `fc:scan`, field = ISO country code, value = count; totals are the sum of fields. The memorial wall uses its own `fc:mem:*` keys in the same database (see Memorial wall). User-facing copy (`rage.countries`, `rage.note`, the privacy section) calls this grouping "region" in every locale; the key `rage.countries` and the code identifiers keep their names. Do not add IPs, ids, timestamps or per-user keys to these two hashes. Rate limiting stays in memory per instance.
- **Provisioning**: the Vercel Marketplace resource is `fuck-claude-stats` (Upstash for Redis, Pay As You Go, no free tier), connected to project `fuck-claude` in all environments. Keep command usage low: reads are CDN-cached (`s-maxage=30`), writes are batched by the client. For local runs, `vercel env pull .env.local` and export the variables into the shell (Astro dev does not fill `process.env` from `.env.local`). Local runs write to the production store. A local request has no `x-vercel-ip-country` header, so a counter write lands in field `XX`; remove that field (`HDEL fc:smash XX`, `HDEL fc:scan XX`) if it appears. Never delete the `fc:smash` or `fc:scan` keys: they hold the live totals.
- **API**: `/api/stats` (`GET` snapshot, `POST { kind, n }`). Without credentials it answers `enabled: false` and the UI shows only the visitor's own count (localStorage `fc:smashes`).
- **Copy**: UI keys are `rage.*` in `src/i18n/ui.ts` (en and zh) with overlays in `src/i18n/messages/<lang>.ts`. The privacy disclosure is `PRIVACY_COUNTERS_SECTION` in `src/content/trust/index.ts`, appended by `resolveTrustPageBody`; its translations live in `src/i18n/translations/<lang>/part-3.ts`. Do not edit the main privacy body text lightly: the dictionary key is the whole English string.

## IP Purity
- **Where**: `/ip/` (`IpPurityPage.astro`), the card on the home page (`IpPurityCard.astro`, client logic `src/scripts/ip-purity-ui.ts`), the endpoint `src/pages/api/ip.ts` and the aggregation in `src/server/ip-purity.ts`.
- **Separate score**: purity is 0-100 (higher = cleaner) and is never added to, averaged with or written into the China-user score. The scored address is the request egress; `?ip=` is ignored.
- **Keys and limits**: `PROXYCHECK_API_KEY` and `ABUSEIPDB_API_KEY` stay in server env and never reach the browser; ipwho.is is only a geo/ASN fallback. The cache (~8 min) and the 30 requests/minute limit are in memory per serverless instance.

## Navigation
- **Registry**: `src/config/nav.ts` exports `NAV_ITEMS` (`as const satisfies readonly NavItemShape[]`). `NavItem` and `NavItemId` are derived from it, so never hand-write an id union. A row is `{ id, path, group: 'tools' | 'explore', labelKey, descKey, footer }`; `path` is the English route and is localized with `localePath(lang, path)`. `SiteHeader.astro` renders both dropdown groups and the mobile panel from it, and `Footer.astro` renders the rows with `footer: true`.
- **Adding a page**: add one registry row, add its `labelKey` and `descKey` (`nav.<name>` and `nav.<name>.desc`; the home row uses `nav.detector`) to `ui.ts` (en and zh) with overlays in the five other locales, and render `<SiteHeader lang={lang} current="<id>" />` in the page shell. No other file lists the pages.
- **Behavior**: the dropdowns and the language switcher are `<details data-nav-menu>`. `src/scripts/nav.ts` closes them on an outside click and on Escape, keeps one open at a time, and closes the mobile panel above 900px. It must not depend on page-specific markup.

## Who am I (`/who-am-i/`)
- **Where**: `WhoAmIPage.astro`; routes `src/pages/who-am-i.astro` and `src/pages/[lang]/who-am-i.astro`; endpoint `src/pages/api/whoami.ts`; client `src/scripts/whoami-collect.ts` (collects readings) and `src/scripts/whoami-ui.ts` (renders); model `src/config/whoami.ts`.
- **Data model**: `READING_DEFS` (27 reading ids in four layers: request, network, script, probe) and `RULES` (8 pure rules, each compares two readings and returns match, mismatch or undecidable) live in `whoami.ts`, which imports no DOM or Astro code so `scripts/whoami-check.mjs` can load it. Findings are heuristics. There is no total score, and nothing is added to the China-user score. UI keys: `whoami.reading.<layer>.<name>`, `whoami.rule.<ruleId>.{title,match,mismatch}`, `whoami.verdict.*`; `npm run whoami:check` fails when a reading or rule has no key. Cards list every finding with a verdict badge, mismatches first; the section title is "Consistency checks", not "Contradictions".
- **Sources**: only what Vercel and the browser provide. `/api/whoami` echoes an allowlist of request headers and the Vercel geo headers (`x-vercel-ip-country`, `-city`, `-timezone`), answers `Cache-Control: private, no-store` and stores nothing. Network type comes from `/api/ip`. JA3/JA4 and TCP fingerprints are not available to Vercel Functions, so they are not shown. A reading that cannot be read is not listed and not labeled.
- **WebRTC probe**: runs only after a click, against `stun:stun.cloudflare.com:3478`. The page makes no other third-party request. Disclosure: `PRIVACY_WHOAMI_SECTION` in `src/content/trust/privacy-whoami.ts`, appended by `resolveTrustPageBody`.

## Memorial wall (`/memorial/`)
- **Where**: `MemorialPage.astro`; routes `src/pages/memorial.astro` and `src/pages/[lang]/memorial.astro`; pure types and validation `src/config/memorial.ts`; store `src/server/memorial-store.ts`; endpoints `src/pages/api/memorial.ts` (`GET` list with `sort=new|long|short`, `cursor`, `limit`; `POST` create), `src/pages/api/memorial/[no].ts` (`PATCH`, `DELETE` with `Authorization: Bearer <edit code>`) and `src/pages/api/memorial/[no]/candle.ts` (`POST`); client `src/scripts/memorial-ui.ts` and `src/scripts/memorial.ts` (localStorage helpers).
- **Data**: an entry is `{ no, createdOn, bannedOn, days, plan: free | pro | max | other, candles, submittedAt }`. There is no free text, email, IP, fingerprint, Anthropic account identifier, payment or KYC field, and none may be added (product owner decision). The edit code is 32 random bytes in base64url, shown once; only its SHA-256 hash is stored and it is compared in constant time. The server validates dates: `createdOn` is not before 2023-03-14 (`CLAUDE_FIRST_RELEASE`, sourced to Anthropic's announcement), `bannedOn` is not before `createdOn` and not after the latest date on Earth (UTC+14). A honeypot field and a minimum fill time reject simple bots.
- **Statistics and copy**: the aggregate has count, mean, median, min, max, candles and 21 quantile points. "Compare my account" is computed in the browser from those quantiles and sends nothing. Copy must say entries are self-reported and unverified, that the numbers are not Anthropic's ban rate, and that Anthropic has not confirmed causes or scale of bans.
- **Storage**: keys are `fc:mem:${VERCEL_ENV || 'development'}:*` in the same Upstash database as the counters, so local runs never touch production entries. Rate limits are in memory per instance and per client address: create 3 per 10 minutes, candle 30 per minute, edit and delete 10 per minute. `scripts/memorial-keys.mjs` builds the key names. `scripts/memorial-admin.mjs` (`stats`, `list`, `hide`, `show`, `delete`, `purge-prefix`) moderates; `purge-prefix` refuses production and production mutators need `--yes`. After local tests run `node scripts/memorial-admin.mjs purge-prefix --env development` with the Upstash variables exported, then `stats` must show an empty aggregate. `npm run memorial:check` covers the validation helpers, `daysBetween`, `percentBelow` and the `memorial.*` UI keys in `ui.en` and `ui.zh`; it does not touch Redis or the endpoints.
- **Dev caching**: the list answers `Cache-Control: public, s-maxage=30, stale-while-revalidate=60`. Vercel consumes `s-maxage` and sends browsers `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` (Vercel docs; not measured on a deployment). The Astro dev server passes the header through unchanged, so Chromium can show a list up to 60 seconds old after you create or delete an entry. The first `/api/memorial` call in a dev session can also take about 2 seconds. When testing locally, wait or fetch with `cache: 'no-cache'` before reporting a missing entry as a bug.

## Detection Signals
- Fingerprint detection signals live in `src/config/signals.ts` with sum of weights = 100.
- Detection must run client-side only without uploading user data. Follow `skills/detection-signals/SKILL.md`.
